@prefix :      <https://thesis.local/kg/portfolio#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

#################################################################
# Portfolio Knowledge Graph — worked ABox, in TriG (explicit named
# graphs), operationalizing 07-ontology-topology.md's partitioning
# scheme against 5 real S&P 500 tickers spanning 5 sectors: AAPL
# (Info Tech), JPM (Financials), XOM (Energy), JNJ (Health Care),
# PG (Consumer Staples). References schema/reference.ttl (asset
# master data, urn:graph:reference — loaded separately, not
# repeated here) and schema/rules.ttl (urn:graph:rules:catalog).
#
# Demonstrates, with internally-consistent numbers a reader can
# check by hand:
#   - VETO_FIN_01 (single-signal) firing for XOM on 2026-08-04.
#   - VETO_COMP_01 (confluent) firing for AAPL on 2026-08-05, with
#     a full RiskEvent/NewsArticle evidence chain.
#   - VETO_RED_01 (contagion) firing for JPM on 2026-08-05, reading
#     XOM's 2026-08-04 primary veto as its T-1 input, via a shared
#     Executive resolved by entity resolution.
#   - VETO_MKT_02 (single-signal, rank 7, added 2026-08-13) firing for XOM on 2026-08-05, via a
#     new SectorRelativeMomentum signal showing XOM badly lagging its (illustratively strong)
#     Energy sector.
#   - AttractivenessSnapshot ranking all 5 tickers on 2026-08-05 — the positive counterpart to
#     veto, computed independently of veto status.
#   - A SECFilingSection restatement (JNJ) via :supersededBy,
#     asserted in the graph where the correction becomes known —
#     not by editing the original graph.
#
# TWO MORE TOPOLOGY ADDENDA found while building this (in addition
# to the reference-graph placement noted in reference.ttl):
#
#   1. Veto/RiskEvent decisions — the Orchestrator's OWN output —
#      needed a graph pattern of their own. 07-ontology-topology.md
#      only named graphs for the four *agents'* daily output.
#      Resolved: urn:graph:ingest:ORCHESTRATOR:{date}, treating the
#      Orchestrator as another daily writer for transaction-time
#      purposes, consistent with the existing per-agent pattern.
#   2. sharedExecutiveWith (entity resolution's output, not an
#      ingestion agent's) gets its own graph too, rather than being
#      folded into an EDGAR ingest graph it didn't come from:
#      urn:graph:derived:entity-resolution:{date}.
#
# NOTE ON RAW VS. NORMALIZED COMPARISON (discovered while picking
# real numbers for this file, not stated in 06-ontology-definition.md):
# Score* metrics (ScoreFinanciero/ScoreTecnico/ScoreCuantitativo) are
# compared via normalizedScore ([0,1], matches v1's 0.65-0.90
# thresholds). Sentiment is compared via rawValue ([-1,1], matches
# v1's -0.50/-0.60 thresholds, which are meaningless on a [0,1]
# scale). The Orchestrator's tree-walker needs this per-metric
# convention hardcoded — flagged here so it isn't lost.
#################################################################

GRAPH <urn:graph:universe:2026-Q3> {
    :SP500Watchlist_2026Q3 a :Universe ; rdfs:label "Fundamental Agent Watchlist, 2026 Q3" .

    :UM_AAPL_2026Q3 a :UniverseMembership ; :membershipAsset :AAPL ; :membershipUniverse :SP500Watchlist_2026Q3 ; :validFrom "2026-07-01"^^xsd:date .
    :UM_JPM_2026Q3  a :UniverseMembership ; :membershipAsset :JPM  ; :membershipUniverse :SP500Watchlist_2026Q3 ; :validFrom "2026-07-01"^^xsd:date .
    :UM_XOM_2026Q3  a :UniverseMembership ; :membershipAsset :XOM  ; :membershipUniverse :SP500Watchlist_2026Q3 ; :validFrom "2026-07-01"^^xsd:date .
    :UM_JNJ_2026Q3  a :UniverseMembership ; :membershipAsset :JNJ  ; :membershipUniverse :SP500Watchlist_2026Q3 ; :validFrom "2026-07-01"^^xsd:date .
    :UM_PG_2026Q3   a :UniverseMembership ; :membershipAsset :PG   ; :membershipUniverse :SP500Watchlist_2026Q3 ; :validFrom "2026-07-01"^^xsd:date .

    :AAPL :hasUniverseMembership :UM_AAPL_2026Q3 .
    :JPM  :hasUniverseMembership :UM_JPM_2026Q3 .
    :XOM  :hasUniverseMembership :UM_XOM_2026Q3 .
    :JNJ  :hasUniverseMembership :UM_JNJ_2026Q3 .
    :PG   :hasUniverseMembership :UM_PG_2026Q3 .
}

